Tile Layer Reliability + One-Way Platform Flow
Summary
Fix multi-layer tile loading so all layers keep their own colliders and alignment, then add explicit per-layer collision policy (solid, one_way, none) with DOWN + JUMP drop-through for one-way platforms.

This addresses your current bug directly:

In PlayState.cpp, tile object names are reused per layer (t0..tN), so later layers overwrite earlier ones in ObjectManager collisions.
In TileMap.h, layer placement metadata (startx/starty/x/y) is not applied, so multi-layer/chunk maps are not fully position-safe.
